                        ],
                        "form": "превра́тности"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "5f92fc1c-1307-48f5-86d1-a02423a41efe",
                        "entry_id": "16c65516-6487-3503-b280-38854dad97d1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "превра́тностях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "20e31f9e-7662-3324-8772-49b709d2f024",
                        "entry_id": "16c65516-6487-3503-b280-38854dad97d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свойство по значению прилагательного превратный; изменчивость, непостоянство"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8317390c-a184-48f9-b1ba-ae1093e3a685",
                                "sense_id": "20e31f9e-7662-3324-8772-49b709d2f024",
                                "text": "Всякая несправедливость к другим может происходить в нас только от двух причин: от незнания или заблуждения нашего рассудка и от превратности воли."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f28cc2bc-06b7-37be-8f74-4fb62f5c4898",
                        "entry_id": "16c65516-6487-3503-b280-38854dad97d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "неожиданная неприятная перемена в жизни, дурной поворот событий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "обычно мн. ч."
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1bc449ad-b9b9-48b9-a8ae-3134930074ac",
                                "sense_id": "f28cc2bc-06b7-37be-8f74-4fb62f5c4898",
                                "text": "Но, приученные жизнью к превратностям и к мысли, что бессмертие ― не их удел, эти, сидящие за столом, с ястребиной зоркостью присматривались друг к другу, не упуская ни одного жеста, ни случайного вздоха, в которых могло бы сквозить хоть малейшее подтверждение печальному несовершенству их судеб и кратковременности земного существования."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9e1d1bf-563c-4989-bbb2-5063cc79cafe",
                                "sense_id": "f28cc2bc-06b7-37be-8f74-4fb62f5c4898",
                                "text": "Да, старик на восьмом десятке может вас уверить, что наука является самой лучшей, прочной, самой светлой опорой в жизни, каковы бы ни были её превратности."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c130309d-08ee-47b9-8413-744fc1ecc2fd",
                        "source_entry_id": "16c65516-6487-3503-b280-38854dad97d1",
                        "source_sense_description": "изменчивость, непостоянство",
                        "target_lang_word": "vicissitude",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vicissitude",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19161463-61d2-3d7e-9ffe-38f78d9e39c4",
                                        "entry_id": "a66bbd91-8d5a-3063-89ef-ad7ee3df6838",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Regular change or succession from one thing to another, or one part of a cycle to the next; alternation; mutual succession; interchange; variability."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51d05497-0a46-336a-983e-7a9b4cc3b011",
                                        "entry_id": "a66bbd91-8d5a-3063-89ef-ad7ee3df6838",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A change, especially in one's life or fortunes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cb090cf-d890-423e-bcbc-e9b4724bba2f",
                                                "sense_id": "51d05497-0a46-336a-983e-7a9b4cc3b011",
                                                "text": "And God made.. the Stars, and set them in the firmament of Heaven to illuminate the Earth, and rule the day in their vicissitude..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "502fb095-c79f-4637-a754-30c89b3136c4",
                                                "sense_id": "51d05497-0a46-336a-983e-7a9b4cc3b011",
                                                "text": "Among the vicissitudes incident to life, no event could have filled me with greater anxieties than that of which the notification was transmitted by your order, and received on the fourteenth day of the present month."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7dcb25cf-4c07-47c9-a42a-3970fdaae40d",
                                                "sense_id": "51d05497-0a46-336a-983e-7a9b4cc3b011",
                                                "text": "The vicissitudes of war in Iraq cast a dreary backdrop for Donald Rumsfeld's first visit to Asian military allies since he became US Defense Secretary in 2001."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "411df119-5b01-44fb-be2e-0661309bf18e",
                                                "sense_id": "51d05497-0a46-336a-983e-7a9b4cc3b011",
                                                "text": "Engaged intellectuals were obliged to take a stand on the side of progress and History, whatever the occasional moral vicissitudes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6209503-8389-4c2f-b813-8b8fa0eef48e",
                                                "sense_id": "51d05497-0a46-336a-983e-7a9b4cc3b011",
                                                "text": "Despite all the monarchy’s vicissitudes, however, Queen Elizabeth II, a figure from another age, who was stiff and formal and not noticeably particularly warm and empathetic, had won and retained the affection, loyalty and support of the overwhelming majority of the British public, who respected her for her diligence and sense of duty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bfdf663d-c17d-4c25-ab21-dcc1d44b11e7",
                        "source_entry_id": "16c65516-6487-3503-b280-38854dad97d1",
                        "source_sense_description": "изменчивость, непостоянство",
                        "target_lang_word": "changeability",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "changeability",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51db246f-f440-308e-85df-89bce6f68967",
                                        "entry_id": "54d1f8aa-03cb-3ba5-86d5-cbf1f10ab858",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being changeable; changeableness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc309a62-9303-4818-8eac-ba6b589de4ff",
                                                "sense_id": "51db246f-f440-308e-85df-89bce6f68967",
                                                "text": "1999, Neil Gaiman, Stardust, page 9 (2001 Perennial Edition).\nIt was chilly that April, with the awkward changeability of English spring."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
